From: Dominique Leuenberger <dimstar@opensuse.org>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 18:45:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Avoid circular macro definition with Flex 2.6.5+

In Flex 2.6.5+, Flex defines YY_BUF_SIZE as (2 * YY_READ_BUF_SIZE).
Defining YY_READ_BUF_SIZE as YY_BUF_SIZE in interact.h creates a
circular macro expansion, causing compilation of lex.yy.cc to fail with:
  error: 'YY_BUF_SIZE' was not declared in this scope

Remove the redundant #define YY_READ_BUF_SIZE YY_BUF_SIZE from interact.h.
---
 interact.h | 2 --
 1 file changed, 2 deletions(-)

diff -up asymptote-3.15/interact.h.orig asymptote-3.15/interact.h
--- asymptote-3.15/interact.h.orig
+++ asymptote-3.15/interact.h
@@ -66,8 +66,6 @@ public:
 
 void setCompleter(completer *c);
 
-#define YY_READ_BUF_SIZE YY_BUF_SIZE
-
 void init_readline(bool tabcompletion);
 }
 
